      "answer": "Here's the trace of what happens when running `ledger --amount 100`:\n\n**Source files involved:**\n\n1. **`src/cli.py`** \u2014 The entry point. Parses `--amount 100`, creates an `InvoiceBuilder`, and calls `builder.build(100)`.\n\n2. **`src/billing/invoice.py`** \u2014 The `InvoiceBuilder.build()` method calls `compute_tax(amount)` and returns `{\"net\": amount, \"tax\": tax, \"gross\": amount + tax}`.\n\n3. **`src/billing/tax.py`** \u2014 The `compute_tax()` function applies the standard rate (0.22) and returns `round(amount * rate, 2)`.\n\n4. **`src/core/config.py`** \u2014 Contains `API_ENDPOINT = \"https://api.example.com/v2\"`, passed to `InvoiceBuilder.__init__()`.\n\n**Computation flow:**\n\n1. `cli.py` parses `--amount 100` \u2192 `args.amount = 100.0`\n2. `InvoiceBuilder.build(100.0)` is called\n3. Inside `build()`, `compute_tax(100.0)` is invoked\n4. In `tax.py`, `STANDARD_RATE = 0.22` is used (since `reduced=False` default), so tax = `round(100.0 * 0.22, 2)` = **22.0**\n5. `build()` returns `{\"net\": 100, \"tax\": 22.0, \"gross\": 100 + 22.0}` \u2192 `\"gross\": 122.0`\n\n**Final gross value printed: `122.0`**",
